## 2. Proto Definition (`proto/account_service.proto`)

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

package account.v1;

option java_multiple_files = true;
option java_package = "com.platform.account.v1";

enum AccountStatus {
  ACCOUNT_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED = 0;
  ACTIVE = 1;
  INACTIVE = 2;
}

message UpdateAccountRequest {
  string account_id = 1;
  // proto3_optional allows tracking field presence (null vs explicitly set)
  optional AccountStatus status = 2;
  optional string display_name = 3;
}

message AccountResponse {
  string account_id = 1;
  AccountStatus status = 2;
  string display_name = 3;
  int64 updated_at = 4;
}

service AccountService {
  rpc UpdateAccount (UpdateAccountRequest) returns (AccountResponse);
}
```

## 3. Data Mapping & Tri-State Strategy
| Request Proto `has_status()` | Request Value | DB Target Action |
|---|---|---|
| `false` (absent / `null`) | N/A | Field ignored; persist existing state |
| `true` | `ACTIVE` | Mutate DB record status to `ACTIVE` |
| `true` | `INACTIVE` | Mutate DB record status to `INACTIVE` |
| `true` | `ACCOUNT_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED` | Return gRPC `Status.INVALID_ARGUMENT` |
```

